{
  "dom_id": "step-e799",
  "name": "Example: Identifying Constants as Like Terms",
  "problem": "What are the like terms of the expression $4 + 0.8p - 2.3p - 3.2p + 10?$",
  "worked_solution": "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(4) + (0.8p) + (-2.3p) + (-3.2p) + (10)\n$$\n\nThere are two groups of like terms:\n\n- $0.8p,$ $-2.3p,$ and $-3.2p$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $p.$\n\n- $4$ and $10$ are like terms because they both contain no variable.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
